<h1>Paul O' Neill: <em>We are all going to make it</em></h1>

<txp:image id="1804" style="float:left;padding-right:10px;padding-bottom:3px;" /><p>Paul O' Neill was NeMe's second artist in residence under the Creative Europe funded <em>European Media Art Platform</em> (EMAP) framework. He was selected from 600 applicants because of his critical approach and the relevance of his proposal to post colonial discourse.</p>

<p>The <em>We are all going to make it</em> artwork, first launched during the <em>Limassol Art Walks</em> on 21st October 2023, is but one of a series he created during his two month residency from May 12 to 14 July 2023.</p>

<p>In the video below, Paul talks about his post-colonial research in Ireland and Cyprus, presented at the NeMe Arts Centre on 7 July 2023.</p>

<iframe class="video" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/BLJq82sEYck" title="Paul O' Neill" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>

<p>You can find out more about the EMAP work curried out by NeNe on the <a href="https://www.neme.org/projects/emap/">NeMe website</a>.</p>

